; Install SAS/C 6.50 into SYS:SC with no person present.
;
; SAS's Commodore Installer script (Install_SASC_6.50 on disk 1) stops at
; its welcome dialog even with MINUSER NOVICE, so this script makes the same
; calls itself. It is the script's hard-disk branch with these choices:
;
;   items      C compiler and headers, optimizers, assembler and headers,
;              debugger, extra utilities, examples and source
;   libraries  standard, IEEE math, 68881 math
;   left out   C++, cross debugger, extras (CED, Enforcer and others), and
;              the on-line help, which would put a 1993 amigaguide.library
;              over the 3.2 one
;
; Every MakeDir and decompress call below is in the order the Installer
; script makes it. The assigns and the path the Installer would add to
; S:User-Startup are written by the recipe instead. The six disks are
; mounted under their own volume names, so nothing asks for a disk swap.

